<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00109">
	<title id="e00766">Removing headrest</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00767">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00768">
								<title>Type A</title>
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV025096.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e00769"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="e00770">
								<title>Type B (GT)</title>
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOVGT025002.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e00771"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>* Before adjusting the headrest, check the lever position for your seat type.</p>
		<p>To remove the headrest:</p>
		<ol>
			<li>
				<p>Recline the seatback with the recline lever or switch.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Push and hold the release button (1). Raise headrest as far as it can go.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<p>Insert a short, flat object (such as a small flat-head screwdriver) into the opening on the inside base of the left post (2) and pull the headrest upward.</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
		<note type="warning">
			<p>NEVER allow anyone to ride in a seat with the headrest removed.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
</concept>